menu "espix audio"

    config ESPIX_AUDIO
        bool "Audio playback (play)"
        depends on ESPIX_BT
        default y
        help
            The play command: esp_audio_simple_dec reads a URI -- a local file
            or an HTTP(S) stream -- decodes it, and hands PCM to the A2DP
            source. On by default where Bluetooth is, and it cannot be anywhere
            else: the engine decodes straight into the A2DP ring, so without
            Bluedroid Classic there is no sink to decode into. The dependency is
            what keeps an S3 -- BLE only -- from linking a decoder it can never
            use, and a stale CONFIG_ESPIX_AUDIO=y in an S3 sdkconfig from
            compiling it anyway.

endmenu
